# 1. using --amend ( changing the commit directly)

---

    Suppose your history is:

    A
    B
    C
    D
    E  ← HEAD

    You want to add changes to commit C.You'll use interactive rebase.

    git rebase -i HEAD~3

    pick C
    pick D
    pick E

    Change it to:

    edit C
    pick D
    pick E

    Save and exit.

    Git rewinds history and stops at C.

    Step 2: Make your changes

    Edit the files.

    Stage them:

    git add .
    git commit --amend

    or
    git commit --amend --no-edit
    Step 4: Continue the rebase
    git rebase --continue

    Git will replay D and E on top of the updated C.
    Final history:

    A
    B
    C'
    D'
    E'

    Notice that C, D, and E all get new commit hashes, because changing C changes the history that follows it.

